Z||000002||StuGood||09-07-2000||06:25 PM||||Agree that Chilton's manuals aren't the best (to date, at least).  Haynes contains more detailed info.<P>If I remember, for the V6 engine, the center pin is only one that runs oil pressure gage.   The outer two pins are a switch that closes when there's (nearly) any oil pressure - acts  as a backup for fuel pump relay.||||reg||1
